MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Otis Redding feels like a natural next choice because his soulful vocals connect with the blues and soul mood I associate with Memphis and Old Sock.",
    "Creedence, the Grateful Dead and Four Tops each connect with parts of my interest in blues, roots rock and soul, even though I would only choose Otis Redding today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Beach Boys' harmony-focused pop and ELO's orchestral rock do not offer the bluesy, soulful sound I want right now, despite some overlap with my interest in older rock.",
    "Definitive Collection gives me no artist to connect with my listening interests, so I cannot judge whether I would enjoy it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some classic rock seems to have been treated as interest in a broad range of older pop and rock, when the sound matters more to me than the era.",
    "Familiar artists and greatest-hits collections seem to recur, but familiarity alone is not enough to make me choose something."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The soulful singing and blues influence that connect Memphis and Old Sock matter more to my choice today than a broad classic-rock connection.",
    "Something can fit my taste without making me want to interact; I rarely choose anything unless it feels especially relevant to my current mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in roots rock and soul, but spread too broadly across older music instead of focusing on the bluesy vocals I want today."
}
